R - RESIDENT DISK RESET

CALLER. Subject to the current caller access policy.

A - Purpose, syntax and examples

:A
R - RESIDENT DISK RESET

CALLER. Subject to the current caller access policy.

Syntax:
    R

Resets CP/M disk state so drives can be logged in again. It does not erase
files. Finish file activity first; use MOUNT for managed collection-volume
changes.

This installed resident token is R. It is different from SYSUTLS:RESET,
which resets the whole emulated machine.

See HELP COMMANDS for the command index.
